The immediate escalation boundary is legitimate: `.slices/0428.slice-md:8,21-23` authorizes the fixture, reference files and narrow AGENTS.md addition, but excludes the production UI file. R0001/R0002 preserve preceding repairs while confining their additional edit authority to 0427. The immutable `S121-COMMITTED-KIT` obligation and `.manual/001` section Q require semantic-message construction and exact bytes. Rewriting fixture slots after construction or ignoring IDs in comparison would violate those requirements. The worker's attempt-02 handoffs, cycle-2 judge and resolver agree with the inspected source. The recommended provider repair is source-traced, **not implemented or runtime-verified here**; pending gates are not the cause.

